        "text": "Constant\nPython does not have immutable variables. For example, in C++, we can specify a const\nkeyword to specify that the variable is immutable and is a constant. Python relies on\nnaming conventions to specify constants. If the code tries to treat a constant as a regular\nvariable, Python will not give an error.\nFor constants, the recommendation is to use uppercase words or words separated by an\nunderscore. An example of a constant is given here:\nCONVERSION_FACTOR\nDeveloping an effective naming scheme     21",
